1          /*******************************************************************************
2          program title: merge_ow_MI.sas
3          Title: Transgenerational, personal, and social determinants of overweight and obesity during childhood and
3        ! adolescence
4          Programmer: Yiqing Wang (nhywa)
5          Template: Klodian Dhana /udd/nhkld/guts/proj2/imputed/5mi/program/  Jie Chen /proj/nhairs/nhair2q/progs/env_htn/
6          Preparation date: 12/2024
7          1) Purpose: Combine multiple imputed datasets and transform wide to long - secondary outcome OWOB
8          2) Study Population:
9          				- NHSII 1995-2013 (for maternal exposures)
10                         - GUTS1 1996-2005 (all offsprings were >=18 by then)
11                         - GUTS2 2004-2013 (all offsprings were >=18 by then)
12         3) Inclusion:
13         	-participants who had exposure and outcome data
14            Exclusion:
15         	-Being obese or having missing BMI at the baseline for personal factors
16         	-BMI measurements excluded if pregnancy/breastfeeding during the past year
17         4) Exposures:
18         	- Maternal obesity, diet quality, physical activity, smoking, drinking, age at birth, Gestational diabetes,
18       ! C-section, Small or large for gestational age
19         	- Offspring diet quality, physical activity, sedentary behavior, Smoking, Drinking, Abnormal sleep duration
20             - Maternal education, Maternal job stress (job strain, rotating night-shift work schedule, job insecurity),
20       ! Neighborhood socioeconomic status,
21         		Number of primary care providers in the county, Food deserts/swamps, Greenspace, Air pollution (personal
21       ! exposure), Summer and winter temperature
22         	- Child abuse (both for the moms and children)
23         	- Yale food addiction scale (NHS2 and later in GUTS)
24         5) Covariates:
25         	- Maternal age at baseline (years), race/ethnicity, maternal total energy intake, maternal chronic diseases (?)
26         	- Offspring age, sex, race/ethnicity, offspring energy intake (?), offspring other chronic diseases (?)
27         6) Statistical analyses: multivariable log-binomial regression models with generalized estimating equations and
27       ! specified an exchangeable correlation structure
28         *******************************************************************************/
29         /* Show full log, try to find which step is the slowest */
30         options msglevel=i fullstimer;
